WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:01.935
Former President Trump says

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:03.303
his 2024 campaign

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:04.838
is going to be focused on the future.

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:06.506
But there are some grievances.

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:08.541
He can't just quit

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:10.777
They're going to restore

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:12.045
election integrity.

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:12.746
We have to

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:13.680
and you go to New York

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.315
nobody ever gets prosecuted.

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:16.316
I'm the only one they go

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:18.084
after I sending people

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:20.086
that are killers murderers.

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:21.187
They're sending rapists

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:23.256
and they're sending, frankly, terrorists.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:24.958
We have a woke military

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:26.760
that can't fight or win

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:27.260
and the wind

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:30.030
turbines are all made in China.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:32.232
They said he's not doing rallies.

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:34.067
He's not campaigning.

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:35.902
Maybe he's lost that step.

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:37.470
We are more angry now

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.371
and I'm more committed

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.440
now than I ever was.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.508
That was not from Trump's

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:43.543
first campaign or his second one.

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:44.911
That was from last weekend.

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:46.413
Several of his allies are telling me

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:47.213
that they're worried he's

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:48.248
stuck in the past

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:49.082
and are concerned

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:51.451
about the viability of his third run.

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:52.652
Their message to him

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:53.887
has been to move forward,

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:55.388
toned down his messages,

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:56.556
stick to the teleprompter

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:57.690
and those speeches.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:58.525
But I'm told he's pushing

00:00:58.525 --> 00:00:59.926
back on that advice, arguing

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:00.560
that he believes

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:01.861
his message is strong enough

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:02.429
and that

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:03.930
he doesn't think any Republicans

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:04.931
should actually challenge him

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:06.166
for the nomination.

00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:06.666
Right now,

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:07.500
he is having a hard time

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.468
convincing some people

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:10.470
to join his campaign, a source says.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:11.871
At least three people have been offered

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:14.107
jobs on the 2020 Ford Trump campaign,

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:15.975
but turned them down, suggesting

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:17.811
maybe they'll join later on.

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:19.512
No one knows more about these dynamics

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:20.880
than CNN's three insiders,

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:21.948
former Illinois Republican

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:23.550
Congressman Adam Kinzinger,

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.184
Alyssa Farah,

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:25.952
who served in the Trump White House,

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:27.220
and, of course, Congressman

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.888
Mondaire Jones from here in New York.

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:31.124
You saw the message.

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:32.725
He said, I'm angrier than ever.

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:33.460
Is that

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.462
is that the start to the 2024

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:36.062
Trump campaign

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:36.729
you think

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:38.498
like it was a funny

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:40.633
quote is not totally scary.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.368
You don't want your elected officials

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:43.703
to be running on a message of

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:44.471
I am angry

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:46.473
and not angry over righteous things

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:47.974
you know poverty homelessness

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:49.809
whatever it might be but angry

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:51.611
because of his own personal grievances

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:53.880
that he didn't win the election in 2020.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.782
This has been a bad launch

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:57.150
from the start for Trump

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.952
and why do you think so.

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:00.053
Low energy

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:02.188
I mean we all watched the launch that day

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:04.357
and it didn't come with a lot of fanfare.

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:05.325
It took him

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:06.392
over two months

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:08.061
to even do a campaign event.

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:09.429
He can't pull the rally events.

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:10.396
You've covered many of them.

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:11.464
I've been to many of them.

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:12.565
He can't pull the audience.

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:13.633
He once did.

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:14.834
But point of caution, he's

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.503
still polling the highest.

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:17.871
And so long as he has that.

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:19.405
30% on lock.

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:20.907
I don't see how anyone can beat him.

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:21.407
What do you think

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:22.142
of how he's returned

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:23.209
to the campaign trail so far?

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:24.677
Because it has been kind of a slow start.

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:25.345
These were his first

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:27.313
really formal events of this year.

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:27.981
Well, he's tired.

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:29.616
He's put on stage.

00:02:29.616 --> 00:02:30.683
I think he is.

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:32.185
He's running the same script.

00:02:32.185 --> 00:02:34.154
There's going to be teleprompter Trump

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:35.922
and then there's off teleprompter Trump.

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:36.856
Teleprompter Trump

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:38.925
may talk a little bit about the future.

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:40.293
Off teleprompter, Trump

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:41.594
will be all about the past.

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:43.096
And I think one of the areas,

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:43.296
you know,

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:45.765
as Alyssa said with this, I'm angry

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:47.300
and all this negativity

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.502
