00:07:16.102 --> 00:07:19.839
You know I really want to defer to

00:07:19.839 --> 00:07:22.642
what makes Biden comfortable on his team

00:07:23.009 --> 00:07:24.610
I've known Kamala for a long time.

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:25.711
I like Kamala.

00:07:25.711 --> 00:07:27.780
I knew her back when she was

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:28.815
when she was attorney

00:07:28.815 --> 00:07:31.651
general and I was still teaching

00:07:31.951 --> 00:07:33.152
and we worked on the housing

00:07:33.152 --> 00:07:34.420
crisis together.

00:07:34.420 --> 00:07:36.322
So we go way back.

00:07:36.322 --> 00:07:38.691
But they need they have to be a team.

00:07:38.691 --> 00:07:40.193
And my sense is they are

00:07:40.193 --> 00:07:41.794
I don't mean that by suggesting I

00:07:41.794 --> 00:07:42.829
think they're in problems.

00:07:44.564 --> 00:07:45.698
That's how the White House took it.

00:07:45.698 --> 00:07:46.866
She later put out a statement

00:07:46.866 --> 00:07:48.501
saying she didn't mean to intend

00:07:48.501 --> 00:07:49.435
or imply that

00:07:49.435 --> 00:07:50.837
she doesn't think they're a great team.

00:07:50.837 --> 00:07:52.338
But that was kind of a moment

00:07:52.338 --> 00:07:54.006
that wasn't as emphatic of endorsement

00:07:54.006 --> 00:07:55.408
as people suspected it might be.

00:07:55.408 --> 00:07:55.575
You know,

00:07:55.575 --> 00:07:56.642
I think people are reading

00:07:56.642 --> 00:07:57.510
too much into it.

00:07:57.510 --> 00:07:58.778
I think she intended

00:07:58.778 --> 00:08:00.213
to do what she said initially,

00:08:00.213 --> 00:08:02.315
which was defer to the president

00:08:02.315 --> 00:08:03.816
I don't think that there is any reason

00:08:03.816 --> 00:08:05.785
that she or anyone else would believe

00:08:05.785 --> 00:08:07.053
that the president

00:08:07.053 --> 00:08:08.221
would not run

00:08:08.221 --> 00:08:09.388
with his vice president

00:08:09.388 --> 00:08:10.756
for a second term.

00:08:10.756 --> 00:08:12.391
And there are concerns within the party.

00:08:12.391 --> 00:08:14.494
I mean, that's that's that's obvious.

00:08:14.494 --> 00:08:16.429
But what I think, you know, people

00:08:16.429 --> 00:08:19.332
wonder about, you know, her popularity.

00:08:19.332 --> 00:08:21.200
But the fact is

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:24.070
she won on the ticket back in 2020.

00:08:24.804 --> 00:08:26.639
If anything, they have more to run on in

00:08:26.639 --> 00:08:28.508
order to be able to,

00:08:28.508 --> 00:08:29.742
you know, survive a challenge

00:08:29.742 --> 00:08:30.643
by Donald Trump

00:08:30.643 --> 00:08:31.944
or I think

00:08:31.944 --> 00:08:32.879
many of the other people

00:08:32.879 --> 00:08:34.213
like Ron DeSantis who are thinking

00:08:34.213 --> 00:08:35.281
about running on the Republican side.

00:08:35.281 --> 00:08:36.249
And I think you'll see that happen.

00:08:36.249 --> 00:08:37.149
Does she help or hurt

00:08:37.149 --> 00:08:38.184
Biden on the ticket?

00:08:39.552 --> 00:08:40.486
I think she helps

00:08:40.486 --> 00:08:42.121
with certain demographics

00:08:42.121 --> 00:08:43.523
and then she's,

00:08:43.523 --> 00:08:44.857
you know, hurtful with respect

00:08:44.857 --> 00:08:45.825
to other demographics.

00:08:45.825 --> 00:08:46.626
But ultimately, it's

00:08:46.626 --> 00:08:47.693
the top of the ticket ticket

00:08:47.693 --> 00:08:48.361
that matters,

00:08:48.361 --> 00:08:50.396
especially when she's clearly qualified,

00:08:50.396 --> 00:08:51.030
unlike a

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:52.565
Sarah Palin who I think was a reason

00:08:52.565 --> 00:08:53.132
why many people

00:08:53.132 --> 00:08:54.834
voted against John McCain.

00:08:54.834 --> 00:08:55.768
Fascinating times.

00:08:55.768 --> 00:08:56.369
Wonder Jones,

00:08:56.369 --> 00:08:57.837
Adam Kinzinger, Alyssa Farah

00:08:57.837 --> 00:08:58.504
Griffin, thank you

00:08:58.504 --> 00:08:59.405
all three for joining us.

